const T_U_SCREEN = "a screen's shape keeps its words and replaces every id, token and code, and a cause is read from the words shown";
const T_U_ONCE = "a link opened counts once per person or device per link, an account before a claim before a device, and nothing else counts once";
const T_U_SETTLED = "a settlement is counted by how it was decided, and a notice's link says its channel before any fragment";
const T_D_RECORD = "a record is a row with its properties and who, a bad property leaves no row and throws nothing, and a link opened counts once per person per link";
const T_D_PATHS = "asking, entering as an account, entering as a guest and a guest bound to an account each leave their row, with what they were and never who they are";
const T_H_DOOR = "the usage door counts a link opened once per device, refuses a link-preview fetcher and every name the browser may not report, and sets the device's cookie";
const ERRORS = "src/lib/ui/errors.ts";
const U_FIELD = "tests/unit/field.test.ts";
const T_U_WRITE = "a write is never shown failed: past ten seconds it is still going with its line, and only a read gets the block with Try again";
const T_U_WORDS = "every cause has its words, each a statement with what to do, and Try again only where a retry could put it right";
const T_U_SIGNED_OUT = "a request that reaches the server as nobody answers the signed-out words from every action, never a thrown error the phone cannot read";
const T_U_MAY_CLOSE = "who may close a market by hand: its asker while it runs, and past its time anyone in it";
const T_U_HASH = "a row's address names the move as a fragment, and a sheet reads it: enter raises the entry, ballot the ballot, close the close's ask";
const T_U_TIMES_UP = "an open market past its close says Time’s up, never Closes soon";
const T_U_START_WORD = "each sport starts in its own word";
const T_U_REMINDER = "the twelve-hour reminder waits for 9am in its zone from 11pm, and the voting notices open the ballot";
const T_U_SESSION = "a session a day old is issued again on the next open, a younger one is left, and none is made from nothing";
const T_U_BAND = "the band's clock is one function for the screen and the shell (3.25, 9.4)";
const T_H_SESSION = "the session slides: a cookie a day old is issued again on a PATCH, a fresh one is left, and no cookie gets none";
const T_D_CLOSE_TWICE = "a second tap on Close finds it closed and is answered as done; before its time nobody but the asker may close it, and the refusal names the asker";
const T_D_VOTING = "voting opened is told once per closed question once it has happened, whichever way, and the reminder is asked for twelve hours into the vote and marked done only once nobody is waiting on their morning";
const T_D_ALL_IN = "the asker hears once when the last person asked is in, never for their own entry, and not while someone is still out";
const T_D_THIRD = "a third person joining a question asked between two makes the set the three of them, never a two-person set with three in it";
const T_D_FOLD = "one guest's entries on two questions fold into one account at sign-in, each kept once at its number";

